      "errorMessage": "<task id=\"ses_f0f9be50affeZkY7rDB3q03g8E\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nI have gathered enough. Here is the structured report.\n\n---\n\n# Report: twenty-front → application logic functions & installed-application detection\n\n## 1. Logic-functions module (`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/logic-functions/`)\n\n### GraphQL operations\n- **Execute mutation** — `packages/twenty-front/src/modules/logic-functions/graphql/mutations/executeOneLogicFunction.ts:3-13`\n  - `EXECUTE_ONE_LOGIC_FUNCTION` (`gql`), `mutation ExecuteOneLogicFunction($input: ExecuteOneLogicFunctionInput!)`, returns `{ data logs duration status error }`.\n  - Input shape (`src/generated-metadata/graphql.ts:1943-1948`): `{ id: UUID!, payload: JSON }`.\n  - Result (`graphql.ts:2471-2490`): `{ data?: JSON, duration: Float, error?: JSON, logs: String, status: LogicFunctionExecutionStatus }`; status enum = `ERROR | IDLE | SUCCESS`.\n- **List query** — `.../graphql/queries/findManyLogicFunctions.ts:4-11`\n  - `FIND_MANY_LOGIC_FUNCTIONS`, `query FindManyLogicFunctions { findManyLogicFunctions { ...LogicFunctionFields } }`.\n  - Fragment `LOGIC_FUNCTION_FRAGMENT` at `.../graphql/fragments/logicFunctionFragment.ts:3-23` (id, name, description, runtime, timeoutSeconds, executionMode, sourceHandlerPath, handlerName, trigger settings, **applicationId**, **universalIdentifier**, createdAt, updatedAt).\n- **Single query** — `.../graphql/queries/findOneLogicFunction.ts:4-11`, variable `LogicFunctionIdInput { id }` (`graphql.ts:2492-2495`).\n- Also present: `createOneLogicFunction.ts`, `updateOneLogicFunction.ts`, `deleteOneLogicFunction.ts`, `getLogicFunctionSourceCode.ts`, `findManyAvailablePackages.ts`.\n- **No `findManyLogicFunctionLogs` query exists in twenty-front.** Logs are delivered by a GraphQL subscription: `Subscription.logicFunctionLogs` / `SubscriptionLogicFunctionLogsArgs` (`graphql.ts:5792`, `5803-5804`). UI component: `src/modules/logic-functions/components/LogicFunctionLogs.tsx:10`.\n\n### Hooks/services\n- **`useExecuteLogicFunction`** — `.../hooks/useExecuteLogicFunction.ts:28-111` (exported).\n  - Signature: `useExecuteLogicFunction({ logicFunctionId: string, callback?: (result: object) => void })`.\n  - Returns `{ executeLogicFunction, updateLogicFunctionInput, logicFunctionTestData, isExecuting }`.\n  - `executeLogicFunction()` takes **no arguments**: it reads the payload from the Jotai family state `logicFunctionTestDataFamilyState` (imported from `@/workflow/workflow-steps/workflow-actions/code-action/states/logicFunctionTestDataFamilyState`, line 4) and calls the mutation with `{ input: { id: logicFunctionId, payload: logicFunctionTestData.input } }` (lines 66-73). This makes it tailored to the settings/workflow \"test function\" UI, not a generic app-function invoker.\n  - It uses the local `EXECUTE_ONE_LOGIC_FUNCTION` gql constant (line 39), **not** the generated `ExecuteOneLogicFunctionDocument`.\n  - Known call sites: `src/modules/settings/logic-functions/components/tabs/SettingsLogicFunctionTestTab.tsx:70`, `src/pages/settings/logic-functions/SettingsLogicFunctionDetail.tsx:70`, `src/modules/workflow/.../code-action/components/WorkflowEditActionCode.tsx:129`, `src/modules/workflow/.../logic-function-action/components/WorkflowEditActionLogicFunction.tsx:144`.\n- **`useGetOneLogicFunction`** — `.../hooks/useGetOneLogicFunction.ts:9-27`: `({ id, skip? })` → `{ logicFunction, loading }`, uses `FIND_ONE_LOGIC_FUNCTION`.\n- **`usePersistLogicFunction`** — `.../hooks/usePersistLogicFunction.ts:25-167`: create/update/delete (settings CRUD); refetches `FIND_MANY_LOGIC_FUNCTIONS`.\n- **`useLogicFunctionThirdPartyApplicationInformation`** — `.../hooks/useLogicFunctionThirdPartyApplicationInformation.ts:12-35`: resolves a logic function's `applicationId` from `logicFunctionsSelector` and returns its app name/chip.\n- **`useGetAvailablePackages`**, `useGetLogicFunctionSourceCode`, `useLogicFunctionForm`, `useLogicFunctionUpdateFormState`.\n\n### State / bulk loading\n- **`logicFunctionsSelector`** — `.../states/logicFunctionsSelector.ts:5-12`: `createAtomSelector<LogicFunction[]>` reading `metadataStoreState, 'logicFunctions'`. This is the front's global list of all logic functions, each carrying `applicationId`, `name`, and `universalIdentifier`.\n- **Type** — `.../types/LogicFunction.ts:3-4`: `FindManyLogicFunctionsQuery['findManyLogicFunctions'][number]`.\n- Bulk load into the metadata store: `src/modules/metadata-store/hooks/useLoadStaleMetadataEntities.ts:175-193` runs `FindManyLogicFunctionsDocument` (`fetchPolicy: 'network-only'`) and calls `replaceDraft('logicFunctions', result.data.findManyLogicFunctions)`. Entity keys registered in `metadata-store/states/metadataStoreState.ts:23` and mapped in `metadata-store/utils/mapAllMetadataNameToEntityKey.ts:16`.\n\n## 2. Applications module (`packages/twenty-front/src/modules/applications/`)\n\n### GraphQL\n- **`findManyApplications`** — `.../graphql/queries/findManyApplications.ts:3-21`: selects `id, name, description, logoUrl, version, state, universalIdentifier, applicationRegistrationId, applicationRegistration { id, latestAvailableVersion, sourceType }`.\n- **`findOneApplication`** — `.../graphql/queries/findOneApplication.ts:4-11` (variable `$id: UUID!`, uses `APPLICATION_FRAGMENT`).\n- **`findOneApplicationByUniversalIdentifier`** — `.../graphql/queries/findOneApplicationByUniversalIdentifier.ts:3-13`: `findOneApplication(universalIdentifier: UUID!) { id universalIdentifier name version state }`.\n- **`APPLICATION_FRAGMENT`** — `.../graphql/fragments/applicationFragment.ts:6-79`: adds `canBeUninstalled, autoUpgrade, defaultRoleId, settingsCustomTabFrontComponentId, availablePackages, applicationVariables, agents, frontComponents, commandMenuItems, objects, logicFunctions {...LogicFunctionFields}`.\n\n### Hooks\n- **`useInstalledApplications`** — `.../hooks/useInstalledApplications.ts:9-33`: runs `FindManyApplicationsDocument`, merges with `applicationsSelector` by id; returns `ApplicationWithoutRelation[]`. Refetches on lifecycle/registration change hooks.\n- **`useIsThirdPartyApplication`** — `.../hooks/useIsThirdPartyApplication.ts:7-25`: looks up `applicationId` in `currentWorkspace?.installedApplications`.\n- **`useApplicationChipData`**, `useApplicationAvatarColors`, `useResolvedApplicationDescription`, `useRefetchOnApplicationLifecycleSettled`, `useRefetchOnApplicationRegistrationChange`.\n- **`applicationsSelector`** — `.../states/applicationsSelector.ts:5-11` → `metadataStoreState, 'applications'` (`FlatApplication[]`).\n- **`ApplicationsLoadEffect`** — `.../components/ApplicationsLoadEffect.tsx:44-117`: network-only `FindManyApplicationsDocument`, maps to `FlatApplication` and `replaceDraft('applications', …)`.\n- **No `useFindManyApplications` and no `useApplicationByRegistrationId` hooks exist** (grep found none). The registration id field is named **`applicationRegistrationId`**, not `registrationId`.\n\n### Record shapes\n- `Application` (`src/generated-metadata/graphql.ts:298-326`): `id, name, description, logoUrl, version, state, universalIdentifier, applicationRegistrationId, applicationRegistration{…}, logicFunctions: LogicFunction[], frontComponents, commandMenuItems, objects, agents, applicationVariables, availablePackages, canBeUninstalled, autoUpgrade, defaultRoleId, settingsCustomTabFrontComponentId, logoFileId, packageJson*, yarnLock*`.\n- `ApplicationWithoutRelation` (`src/pages/settings/applications/types/applicationWithoutRelation.ts:3-13`): Pick of `id, name, description, logoUrl, version, universalIdentifier, applicationRegistrationId, applicationRegistration`.\n- `FlatApplication` (`src/modules/metadata-store/types/FlatApplication.ts:3-12`): Pick of `id, universalIdentifier, name, description, version, state, applicationRegistrationId`.\n\n## 3. How the front determines whether an app is installed\n\n- **`findManyApplications` is install-scoped.** Server resolver `packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/application/application-install/application-install.resolver.ts:72-78` → `ApplicationService.findManyApplications` (`application.service.ts:153-160`) queries `applicationRepository.find({ where: { workspaceId }, relations: ['applicationRegistration'] })`. So *presence in `findManyApplications` = installed in this workspace*.\n- **Canonical front pattern** — `src/modules/a2e-workspace/hooks/useA2eSuiteApplications.ts:15-56`:\n  - builds `installedUniversalIdentifiers` = `Set(data.findManyApplications.map(a => a.universalIdentifier))` (lines 27-35);\n  - `installedApplications` = `findManyApplications` filtered to the A2E suite universal-identifier list (lines 37-45);\n  - `availableApplications` = marketplace catalog (`useMarketplaceApps`) minus `installedUniversalIdentifiers` (lines 47-54).\n  - Comment at lines 12-14 states the identity rule: \"`findManyApplications` holds workspace installs only… whose app id **IS** the application universal identifier.\"\n- **Existence check alternative**: `findOneApplication(universalIdentifier)` (`findOneApplicationByUniversalIdentifier.ts`), used e.g. in `src/pages/settings/applications/SettingsAvailableApplicationDetails.tsx:63`.\n- **Auth-state alternative**: `currentWorkspace?.installedApplications` (e.g. `useIsThirdPartyApplication.ts:16`, `pages/settings/ai/utils/getToolApplicationId.ts:15`, `pages/settings/data-model/SettingsObjectTable.tsx:95`).\n- Stable identity for matching is `universalIdentifier`; `applicationRegistrationId` links an install to its registration/publisher record. The A2E app UIDs are hard-coded in `src/modules/a2e-workspace/constants/A2eSuiteApplicationUniversalIdentifiers.ts:5-17`.\n\n## 4. Existing examples of the front calling an app-provided logic function\n\n- **None for app functions such as `list-template-descriptors`.** A repo-wide search for `list-template-descriptors` hits only the four app packages (`packages/twenty-apps/internal/{a2e-documents,a2e-projects,a2e-accounting,a2e-drive}/src/logic-functions/list-template-descriptors.ts`) plus docs/ralph logs — **zero hits under `packages/twenty-front/src`**.\n- The descriptor function is a plain `defineLogicFunction` handler, e.g. `packages/twenty-apps/internal/a2e-documents/src/logic-functions/list-template-descriptors.ts:12-22`, name `'list-template-descriptors'`, returns `{ templates: buildDocumentTemplateDescriptors() }`, no `toolTriggerSettings`.\n- The only front-side execution path is the generic `useExecuteLogicFunction` mutation by logic-function `id` (Section 1). To execute an app function the front must first resolve its id, e.g. filter `logicFunctionsSelector` by `applicationId` + `name` (the selector fields support this), then call `executeOneLogicFunction`. No helper doing this lookup exists yet.\n- A separate, non-Apollo path exists for **app front-components**: `FrontComponentRenderer` passes `functionsBaseUrl` (from `useGetLogicFunctionHttpUrl`, `src/modules/settings/logic-functions/hooks/useGetLogicFunctionHttpUrl.ts:12-39`; base `/s` or `https://<subdomain>.<publicFunctionDomain>`, util `utils/getLogicFunctionHttpUrl.ts:3-42`) into `twenty-front-component-renderer`, so app code calls logic functions over HTTP route triggers, not through the front's GraphQL mutation.\n- Server-side executors for reference: `ApplicationInstallService`, `LogicFunctionExecutorService` (`packages/twenty-server/src/engine/core-modules/logic-function/logic-function-executor/logic-function-executor.service.ts:81`), and resolver `logic-function.resolver.ts:177-194` (`executeOneLogicFunction`, guarded by `SettingsPermissionGuard(PermissionFlagType.WORKFLOWS)`; note both `executeOneLogicFunction` mutation and `findManyLogicFunctions` query in the front run against the **metadata** schema).\n\n## 5. Generated GraphQL document-hook mechanism\n\n- **Codegen configs**: `packages/twenty-front/codegen.cjs` (core/data), `codegen-metadata.cjs` (metadata), `codegen-admin.cjs` (admin). Metadata config `codegen-metadata.cjs`:\n  - schema = `${REACT_APP_SERVER_BASE_URL ?? 'http://localhost:3000'}/metadata` (lines 4-6);\n  - `documents` globs include `./src/modules/applications/graphql/**/*.{ts,tsx}` (line 12) and `./src/modules/logic-functions/graphql/**/*.{ts,tsx}` (line 23), plus `./src/modules/settings/**/graphql/**` and `./src/pages/**/graphql/**` (lines 18, 48), excluding tests/stories/mocks (lines 50-52);\n  - output `./src/generated-metadata/graphql.ts` with plugins `typescript`, `typescript-operations`, `typed-document-node` (lines 55-67).\n- **Commands** (`packages/twenty-front/project.json:252-270`): `graphql:generate` runs `dotenv graphql-codegen -- --config={args.config}`, configurations `data` (default) / `metadata` / `admin`. Per `AGENTS.md`: `npx nx run twenty-front:graphql:generate` (add `--configuration=metadata` for the metadata schema).\n- **Workflow to add a query/mutation**: add a `.ts` file exporting `gql` under a scanned `graphql/` directory → run codegen → a typed `XDocument` (and `XQuery`/`XVariables` types) is emitted into `src/generated-metadata/graphql.ts` → import the `Document` and types and pass to Apollo `useQuery`/`useMutation`.\n- **Generated docs already emitted** (in `src/generated-metadata/graphql.ts`):\n  - `ExecuteOneLogicFunctionDocument` — line 9777; `ExecuteOneLogicFunctionMutation` type line 8057.\n  - `FindManyLogicFunctionsDocument` — line 9780; `FindManyLogicFunctionsQuery` line 8076.\n  - `FindOneLogicFunctionDocument` — line 9781.\n  - `FindManyApplicationsDocument` — line 9722; `FindManyApplicationsQuery` line 7515.\n  - `FindOneApplicationDocument` — line 9723; `FindOneApplicationByUniversalIdentifierDocument` — line 9724.\n- **Usage conventions differ by module**: applications hooks import generated documents directly (`useInstalledApplications.ts:6`, `ApplicationsLoadEffect.tsx:14-17`, `useA2eSuiteApplications.ts:4-8`); the logic-functions execute hook still uses its hand-written `gql` constant (`useExecuteLogicFunction.ts:1,39`) even though `ExecuteOneLogicFunctionDocument` exists.\n\n## Bottom line\n- Installed apps are known via `findManyApplications` (workspace-scoped = installed), exposed through `useInstalledApplications`, `applicationsSelector`, `ApplicationsLoadEffect`, and `useA2eSuiteApplications`, keyed by `universalIdentifier`; `findOneApplication(universalIdentifier)` is the existence check.\n- The only front call to run a logic function is the `executeOneLogicFunction` mutation, wrapped by `useExecuteLogicFunction({ logicFunctionId, callback? })`, which is currently built for settings/workflow test payloads and takes no payload argument.\n- There is **no existing front example** of invoking an app-provided function like `list-template-descriptors`; doing so would require resolving the function id from `logicFunctionsSelector` by `applicationId`/`name` and then calling the mutation (or using the front-component HTTP/SDK path for app-rendered components).\n</task_result>\n</task>",
