uences for a gallery \"Use template\" action\n\n- **The descriptor layer and the write layer are not connected in any app.** The descriptors are pure data with a declared `preview`; only `a2e-documents` even has a working copy implementation, and it is keyed by a live `document` record id fetched from the tree, not by descriptor `key`.\n- To make \"Use template\" trigger \"the existing template path\", the gallery would need, per app:\n  - a2e-documents: a callable apply that resolves `key → STARTER_DOCUMENT_TEMPLATES[i]` (or a pre-seeded TEMPLATE record) and persists via `buildTemplateCopyPayload`; today only the front-component does this by id.\n  - a2e-projects: no existing path — would require extracting the `createStarterProject` logic from `post-install.ts:43` into a callable handler accepting a template `key`.\n  - a2e-accounting: no existing path — would require extracting `seedStarterFiches`/`withTemplateDefaults` into a callable handler accepting a `FicheTemplateKey` (note only 2 of 10 keys are seeded; the other 8 exist only as descriptors).\n  - a2e-drive: no existing path — would require exposing `createTemplateTree`/`seedFolderStructures` for a single template `key`.\n- None of the four `list-template-descriptors` handlers accept any input (no template key), so the gallery currently has a read side only. Related plan references: `PLAN.md:82` (M9 planned), `PLAN.md:329-371` (M9 scope incl. \"Use template\"), `tasks/prd.json:359-367` (US-118 AC), `docs/plan/phases/phase-13-report.md:150-177` (US-117 shipped the descriptors and the shared contract; `package.json` bumps match the versions above).\n</task_result>\n</task>"
